```apex
public with sharing class ContactDomainService {

    /**
     * Returns contacts of the given accounts grouped by the lower-cased
     * domain portion of their email.  Contacts with no email (or no
     * extractable domain) are excluded.  A null / empty set yields an
     * empty map.  Only Id, Email and AccountId are queried.
     */
    public static Map<String, List<Contact>> groupByEmailDomain(Set<Id> accountIds) {
        Map<String, List<Contact>> result = new Map<String, List<Contact>>();

        // Guard: null or empty input → empty map
        if (accountIds == null || accountIds.isEmpty()) {
            return result;
        }

        // Single bulk-safe query, sharing enforced by "with sharing" on the class.
        // Only the three required fields are retrieved.
        List<Contact> contacts = [
            SELECT Id, Email, AccountId
            FROM   Contact
            WHERE  AccountId IN :accountIds
              AND  Email != null
        ];

        for (Contact c : contacts) {
            String email = c.Email;

            // Skip blank emails or emails that contain no '@' separator
            if (String.isBlank(email) || !email.contains('@')) {
                continue;
            }

            String domain = email.substringAfter('@').toLowerCase();

            // Skip cases like "jane@" where the domain portion is empty
            if (String.isBlank(domain)) {
                continue;
            }

            List<Contact> bucket = result.get(domain);
            if (bucket == null) {
                bucket = new List<Contact>();
                result.put(domain, bucket);
            }
            bucket.add(c);
        }

        return result;
    }
}
```

**Design notes:**

| Concern | How it is addressed |
|---|---|
| **Sharing** | `with sharing` on the class ensures the running user's OWD / sharing rules are respected; no `Without Sharing` anywhere. |
| **Bulk-safety** | A single SOQL query retrieves all contacts. No DML in a loop; no per-account queries. The `IN :accountIds` filter uses a `Set<Id>` which is the recommended pattern. |
| **Field selection** | Only `Id`, `Email`, `AccountId` are queried, guaranteeing those three fields are populated on every returned record while keeping the query lightweight. |
| **Null / empty input** | Early return of an empty `Map` before any query executes. |
| **Email domain extraction** | `substringAfter('@')` + `toLowerCase()` gives e.g. `example.com` for `Jane@Example.COM`. Contacts whose email is null, blank, missing `@`, or whose domain portion is blank after the `@` are silently skipped. |
| **Grouping** | A standard "check-then-create-list" pattern keeps the inner loop at O(1) per contact. |

