### Key design decisions

| Requirement | How it's met |
|---|---|
| Every editor validated (no short-circuit) | `forEach` is used instead of `every()`, so the loop visits **all** children regardless of earlier failures. |
| `submit` event dispatched only when all valid | `allValid` flag is set during the validation pass; the dispatch happens inside the `if (allValid)` block. |
| Error `<p>` shown / hidden reactively | A simple boolean `showError` toggled in the handler drives `<template if:true={showError}>`. It is reset to `false` on a successful submit so the message disappears. |
| Display order preserved | `querySelectorAll` on a `for:each` returns nodes in DOM order; `Array.from(editors).map(…)` produces the `lines` array in the same order. |
| Child receives its data | `item={line}` passes the whole `{ key, productName, quantity }` object to the child's `@api item` property. |

