| Bug | Root cause | Fix |
|---|---|---|
| Heading upper-casing lost on parent re-set | `connectedCallback` mutated the `@api` property itself | Replaced with a getter/setter pair storing the raw value in `_heading`; template renders a separate `displayHeading` getter |
| Parent's array / task objects mutated | `this.items = this.tasks` aliased the reference; `push` / property writes hit the parent's objects | `tasks` setter maps to a fresh array of spread-copied task objects |
| Parent changes to `tasks` ignored | Only read once in `connectedCallback` | Setter is invoked every time the parent rebinds, rebuilding `items` |
| Ticking a checkbox did nothing / threw | `task.done = !task.done` mutates a property on an object inside the array — LWC doesn't track that | Replace the whole element: `this.items[index] = { ...task, done: !task.done }` |
| Added tasks not rendered | `push` on an array that was a direct reference to the parent's `@api` array could desync reactivity | `items` is always our own array; `push` on it triggers LWC reactivity correctly |
| `taskadded` event never reached parent | Event name `'taskAdded'` (camelCase) is invalid in LWC; also `detail.label` was empty (read *after* clearing `newLabel`) | Lowercase `'taskadded'`; capture `label` in a local const before resetting `newLabel` |
| Whitespace-only labels added | No trim / guard | `label.trim()` checked before any push or dispatch |

