public class HouseholdService {

    public static Id createHousehold(List<Contact> members) {
        if (members == null || members.isEmpty()) {
            throw new IllegalArgumentException('members list must not be null or empty');
        }

        // Resolve the Household Account record type without hard-coding an Id
        RecordType hhRt = Schema.SObjectType.Account.getRecordTypeInfosByDeveloperName().get('HH_Account');
        if (hhRt == null || !hhRt.isAvailable()) {
            throw new IllegalStateException('Household Account record type (HH_Account) not found or inactive.');
        }

        // 1. Create the NPSP household account.
        //    Do NOT set Name – NPSP's automatic household naming / greeting
        //    logic (Contact after-insert trigger) populates it once members exist.
        Account household = new Account(
            RecordTypeId = hhRt.getRecordTypeId()
        );
        insert household;

        // 2. Point every contact at the new household so NPSP does NOT
        //    auto-create additional households during contact insert.
        for (Contact c : members) {
            c.AccountId = household.Id;
        }
        insert members;

        // 3. Mark the first contact as the household's primary contact.
        //    NPSP expects the field to be populated after contacts exist.
        household.Primary_Contact__c = members[0].Id;
        update household;

        return household.Id;
    }
}
```

**Key design decisions**

| Concern | How it is addressed |
|---|---|
| Real NPSP household | Insert uses the `HH_Account` record type so NPSP's `Contact` triggers fire household-naming and greeting generation. |
| Name not set by us | The `Account` is inserted with only `RecordTypeId`; NPSP's after-insert logic on the contact records populates `Name` and `__r.npe01__…` greeting fields. |
| No extra / empty accounts | `AccountId` is assigned **before** the contact DML, preventing NPSP's "auto-create household" path. If any step throws, the whole transaction rolls back (no save-points, no partial commits), so the just-created Account is undone. |
| No hard-coded record-type Ids | Resolved at runtime via `Schema.SObjectType.Account.getRecordTypeInfosByDeveloperName()` (metadata cache, zero SOQL, bulk-safe). |
| Primary contact | Set on the Account via `Primary_Contact__c` (NPSP field, no namespace in current 2-GP releases). |
| Bulk-safe | Exactly 3 DML operations (1 Account insert, 1 Contact insert, 1 Account update) regardless of list size. |
| Null / empty guard | Throws `IllegalArgumentException` before any DML runs. |

