```apex
public class PaymentPlanService {

    public class PaymentPlanException extends Exception {}

    public static List<npe01__OppPayment__c> scheduleInstallments(
        Id opportunityId,
        Integer numberOfPayments,
        Date firstPaymentDate
    ) {
        // ── Validate numberOfPayments (before any DML) ──
        if (numberOfPayments == null || numberOfPayments < 1) {
            throw new PaymentPlanException(
                'numberOfPayments must be at least 1.'
            );
        }

        // ── Retrieve the opportunity ──
        Opportunity opp = [
            SELECT Id, Amount, IsClosed
            FROM Opportunity
            WHERE Id = :opportunityId
            FOR UPDATE
            LIMIT 1
        ];

        // ── Validate opportunity is not closed (before any DML) ──
        if (opp == null || opp.IsClosed) {
            throw new PaymentPlanException(
                'Cannot schedule installments on a closed opportunity.'
            );
        }

        // ── Query every payment already associated with this opportunity ──
        List<npe01__OppPayment__c> existingPayments = [
            SELECT
                Id,
                npe01__Payment_Amount__c,
                npe01__Paid__c,
                npe01__Written_Off__c
            FROM npe01__OppPayment__c
            WHERE npe01__Opportunity__c = :opportunityId
        ];

        // ── Separate history (paid ∪ written-off) from active (replaceable) ──
        List<npe01__OppPayment__c> paymentsToDelete = new List<npe01__OppPayment__c>();
        Decimal historyAmount = 0;

        for (npe01__OppPayment__c p : existingPayments) {
            if (p.npe01__Paid__c || p.npe01__Written_Off__c) {
                // This is a paid or written-off payment – count it toward history
                historyAmount += (p.npe01__Payment_Amount__c != null
                    ? p.npe01__Payment_Amount__c
                    : 0);
            } else {
                // Unpaid AND not written off – will be deleted
                paymentsToDelete.add(p);
            }
        }

        // ── Compute outstanding balance ──
        Decimal oppAmount = opp.Amount != null ? opp.Amount : 0;
        Decimal outstanding = oppAmount - historyAmount;

        // ── Validate outstanding > 0 (before any DML) ──
        if (outstanding <= 0) {
            throw new PaymentPlanException(
                'Outstanding amount is not greater than zero.'
            );
        }

        // ── Build the new installment payments ──
        Decimal installment = (outstanding / numberOfPayments)
            .setScale(2, RoundingMode.DOWN);

        List<npe01__OppPayment__c> newPayments = new List<npe01__OppPayment__c>(
            numberOfPayments
        );

        for (Integer i = 0; i < numberOfPayments; i++) {
            newPayments.add(new npe01__OppPayment__c(
                npe01__Opportunity__c     = opportunityId,
                npe01__Payment_Amount__c  = installment,
                npe01__Paid__c            = false,
                npe01__Written_Off__c     = false,
                npe01__Payment_Due_Date__c = firstPaymentDate.addMonths(i)
            ));
        }

        // ── Last payment absorbs the rounding remainder ──
        Decimal sumOfFirstNMinus1 = installment * (numberOfPayments - 1);
        newPayments[newPayments.size() - 1].npe01__Payment_Amount__c =
            outstanding - sumOfFirstNMinus1;

        // ── DML: delete old active payments, insert new ones ──
        if (!paymentsToDelete.isEmpty()) {
            delete paymentsToDelete;
        }
        insert newPayments;

        return newPayments;
    }
}
```

**Key design decisions and notes:**

| Concern | How it's handled |
|---|---|
| **History preservation** | Payments where `npe01__Paid__c = true` **or** `npe01__Written_Off__c = true` are never deleted and their amounts are subtracted from the opportunity's total to derive the outstanding balance. |
| **Rounding & remainder** | Each installment is `outstanding / n` rounded **DOWN** to 2 decimal places (`RoundingMode.DOWN`). The **last** payment is set to `outstanding − installment × (n−1)`, so the series sums to exactly the outstanding amount. |
| **Atomicity / "without changing anything"** | All three validation checks (`numberOfPayments`, closed opportunity, outstanding ≤ 0) run **before** any DML. If a `PaymentPlanException` is thrown, the org is untouched. |
| **Bulk safety** | The existing payments are fetched with a single SOQL query. `FOR UPDATE` on the Opportunity locks the parent row to prevent concurrent scheduling races. Delete and insert are each a single DML statement—no DML inside loops. |
| **Null-amount safety** | Both `opp.Amount` and individual `npe01__Payment_Amount__c` values are guarded against `null`. |
| **Return value** | The list is built in schedule order (index 0 → index *n*−1) and returned directly after insertion, so the caller gets the records with their new `Id` values. |

