## Analysis

The `orgPreferences` key was deprecated in scratch org definition files. The modern equivalent is the `settings` object, which uses the same field names you'd see in the Metadata API Settings types (e.g., `lightningExperienceSettings`, `chatterSettings`, etc.).

Preference → Settings mapping:

| Preference | Settings type | Field | Value |
|---|---|---|---|
| `S1DesktopEnabled` (enabled) | `lightningExperienceSettings` | `enableS1DesktopEnabled` | `true` |
| `S1EncryptedStoragePref2` (disabled) | `lightningExperienceSettings` | `enableSecureStorageEnabled` | `false` |
| `ChatterEnabled` (enabled) | `chatterSettings` | `enableChatter` | `true` |
